# src/apps/daemon/internal/foundation/capabilities

## Purpose
Capability/workflow registry and availability classification used to keep public capability truth explicit.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `foundation` (rank 0; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (5): `capabilities_test.go`, `registry.go`, `route_gate.go`, `route_gate_test.go`, `workflows.go`

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `capabilities`.
- Notable exported surface: `Capability`, `CapabilityID`, `GetWorkflowForRoute`, `GuardRoute`, `Maturity`, `NewRegistry`, `Registry`, `WorkflowID`.
- Daemon-local dependencies: none.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `internal/adapters/api`.

## Invariants
- Capability truth distinguishes implemented/available from unavailable, degraded, simulated, or unverified behavior.
- `foundation` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
